Alternative for GRA-06: reject an else-less conditional ordering strategy
instead of defaulting to the identity ordering. Rejected: ordering needs a
result, and existing user strategies that omit the else branch (a documented
no-op in mapping/separation) would start to fail. Shown for hgraphOrderSt only.

--- a/src/libscotch/hgraph_order_st.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/hgraph_order_st.c
@@ hgraphOrderSt STRATNODECOND else branch @@
         else {                                    /* Else if expression is false             */
           if (straptr->data.conddat.stratab[1] != NULL) /* And if there is an else statement */
             o = hgraphOrderSt (grafptr, ordeptr, ordenum, cblkptr, straptr->data.conddat.stratab[1]);
+          else {                                  /* Else no strategy to apply */
+            errorPrint ("hgraphOrderSt: conditional ordering strategy requires an else branch");
+            o = 1;
+          }
         }
